    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0437" n="325" xml:id="pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.51/303</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-06T12:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 5, 6 p.m. From previous conversation with Foreign Minister, and from
                    his written statement contained in my March 19, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d360-f1"/> Cuban Government understands authority given Cuban
                    Minister in document transmitted in my March 13, midnight,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d360-f2"/> to be complete and absolute. Please, therefore, express
                    exactly the additional form desired so I may ask for it. Legation has not the
                    act of Congress of April 24, 1917.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
